  "headline": "2.2 MMcfd filed on 52 leases with a surface well (14 oil leases and 38 gas wells). Circle size follows that filing.",
  "method": "Volumes are the vented-or-flared column on the Railroad Commission Form PR tapes posted September 26, 2026. The tape still has one column for that disposition. It does not split flare from vent. Each lease is its latest month on the tape. MMcfd is that month's Mcf divided by the days in the month, then by 1,000. The circle is the centroid of RRC surface wells on that lease, joined through the 2026-09-23 API extract. A well is kept only when the lease name on the API record matches the name on the production filing. Pipelines are the EIA centerline compilation from January 2020, clipped to the bounding box of these counties. Transmission lines are the public 230 kV-and-above subset in the project database. Tie-ins are midpoints of those lines within 3 miles of a gas pipeline midpoint, kept when the point is inside one of these counties. Points of interconnection are substations and taps of 69 kV and above inside these counties. The utility name is the owner on an in-service line within half a mile. This view is Texas only. Counties drawn: Harris, Galveston, Brazoria, Chambers, Jefferson, Orange, Liberty, Hardin, Jasper, Newton, Matagorda, Wharton, Fort Bend, Calhoun, Jackson."
}